# GeT-RM reference material, Coriell ID HG00118 (British from England and
# Scotland, 1000 Genomes). GeT-RM genotype-level data (Tier1_c.1129-5923C>G
# = C/G heterozygous; Tier1_c.2846A>T = A/T heterozygous; all other Tier 1
# positions homozygous reference) retrieved via Coriell's GeT-RM PGx Search
# tool (https://www.coriell.org/GeTRM/PGxSearch, gene=DPYD), 2026-08-17.
# Source study: Gaedigk A et al., "Characterization of Reference Materials
# for DPYD: A GeT-RM Collaborative Project." J Mol Diagn 2024;26:864-875
# (PMID 39032822).
#
# A genuinely valuable real-world case, not constructed to be interesting:
# HG00118 carries real heterozygous variants at TWO independent DPYD loci
# simultaneously (HapB3-intronic and D949V). Per genes/dpyd.py's documented
# scope limitation, this project does not attempt multi-locus phasing and
# correctly reports UNSUPPORTED_ALLELE rather than guessing which haplotype
# each variant sits on. See docs/VALIDATION.md.
#
# HapB3 exonic tag (c.1236G>A) genotype for this sample was not retrieved
# this session (browser-tool instability cut off data collection before
# this column could be confirmed) -- represented as a no-call below rather
# than fabricated. This does not affect the result: HapB3-intronic is
# observed and confidently called, so it is authoritative regardless of the
# exonic tag's status (see _call_hapb3_zygosity in genes/dpyd.py).
